  "narrative": {
    "intro": "The Department of Agriculture has $6.7B in contract obligations for FY2026 to date. Obligations fell 30.0% year over year. The agency has made 18,184 awards so far, and the average award size is $368K. FY2026 to date is lower than prior full fiscal years, following $9.6B in FY25, $11.6B in FY24, $11.5B in FY23, $10B in FY22, and $9.7B in FY21. Spending in FY2026 to date is concentrated in food and logistics industries as well as IT and forestry support. The largest category by obligations is Nonscheduled Chartered Freight Air Transportation at $724M, followed by Highway, Street, and Bridge Construction at $439M, and Animal (except Poultry) Slaughtering at $416M. Top vendors by obligations include KIEWIT INFRASTRUCTURE SOUTH CO at $261M, TYSON FOODS INC. at $158M, and PALANTIR TECHNOLOGIES INC. at $129M. These totals are contract obligations and the current-year figures are partial, fiscal year to date.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How does FY2026 to date compare with recent years?",
        "body": "FY2026 to date obligations are $6.7B, which is below the prior full-year totals. FY25 was $9.6B, FY24 was $11.6B, FY23 was $11.5B, FY22 was $10B, and FY21 was $9.7B. Obligations fell 30.0% year over year. The current total reflects partial, fiscal year to date obligations."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Where is Agriculture spending its contract dollars?",
        "body": "The largest NAICS category in FY2026 to date is Nonscheduled Chartered Freight Air Transportation at $724M. Other major categories include Highway, Street, and Bridge Construction at $439M, Animal (except Poultry) Slaughtering at $416M, and Fruit and Vegetable Canning at $397M. Top vendors include KIEWIT INFRASTRUCTURE SOUTH CO at $261M and TYSON FOODS INC. at $158M."
      }
    ]
  },
