      "q": "How much does Department of Agriculture spend on contracts?",
      "a": "The Department of Agriculture has $6.7B in contract obligations for FY2026 to date. That total comes from 18,184 awards with an average award size of $368K. FY2026 to date obligations are down 30.0% year over year, and the current-year total is partial, fiscal year to date."
    },
    {
      "q": "What does Agriculture buy?",
      "a": "Agriculture buys a mix of food processing and logistics, construction, IT services, and forestry support. Leading NAICS categories in FY2026 to date include Nonscheduled Chartered Freight Air Transportation at $724M, Highway, Street, and Bridge Construction at $439M, Animal (except Poultry) Slaughtering at $416M, and Fruit and Vegetable Canning at $397M."
